{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bfopqazfks433azbhukyn54b2jroumbrlzgpie4llwlqycjwqxqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete. No divergence found in the translation** — `src/lib.rs` needed no behavioral fixes.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — 0 missing symbols in Rust `.so` | ✅ both export exactly `driver` |\n| Phase B — all 16 `CONFIGS.md` rows, randomized | ✅ ~4000 input pairs, fixed seed |\n| Binary stdout comparison | N/A — neither build produces an executable |\n| Phase C — all 12 `ERRORS.md` rows | ✅ |\n| Every feature combination | ✅ 6 combos: {release, debug} × {default, no-default, all} → `ALL COMBINATIONS PASSED` |\n\n## What I found (two harness defects, not library bugs)\n\nBoth initially produced **wrong results**, so they matter:\n\n1. **`cargo test` never rebuilt the cdylib.** An integration test that only `dlopen`s the `.so` creates no build dependency on it. `cargo test` refreshes `target/<profile>/deps/libdriver.so` but leaves the top-level `target/<profile>/libdriver.so` hardlink stale — my first mutation run reported 14/14 \"kills\" that were entirely spurious (it was loading a mutant that was never replaced). Fixed with `crate-type = [\"cdylib\", \"rlib\"]`, newest-candidate path resolution, and an mtime staleness assertion.\n2. **fd 1 is process-global.** libtest's own progress banner landed inside the stdout capture window under default thread parallelism, producing 4 bogus \"divergences\". Fixed by running each phase's rows from one sequential `#[test]` and flushing Rust's `Stdout` before each capture.\n\n## Trustworthiness evidence\n\n`./mutation_check.sh`: **null mutant survives, 14/14 real mutants killed** — covering every condition (`x>0||y>0`, `x==1&&y==4`, `x>0`, `y==0`, `x<3`), both decrements, all three printed literals, and the `skip_label1` reset. Plus in-test non-vacuity guards: E9 has a positive control that must be *observed to terminate*; E10 requires ≥32 KiB of comparable output.\n\n## Notable C behaviors replicated rather than \"fixed\"\n\n- The `x == 1 && y == 4` test is evaluated **once per `while` iteration** — the backwards `goto label1` jumps past it. The Rust `skip_label1` flag reproduces this exactly.\n- `y < 0` with `x > 0` **never terminates** in C (`y--` never hits 0). Tested as a matching non-termination via child processes under timeout, not \"fixed\".\n- `wrapping_sub` for `x--`/`y--`: unreachable in any terminating run, but it keeps the `debug` profile from panicking where C would not.\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `tests/{configs,errors,symbols}.rs`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, `run_all_combos.sh`, `mutation_check.sh`. `c_src/` untouched apart from the gitignorable `build/` output.\n\nOne thing to flag: I set `net.offline = true` in `translation/.cargo/config.toml` because the sandbox blocks crates.io; `libloading 0.8.9` resolved from the local cargo cache. Remove that file if you build somewhere with network access."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":734,"cache_read_input_tokens":115058,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":734,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2603bb2a-573d-41ca-b327-f7449802070e","uuid":"8dc637a2-e998-4477-86ee-a1b7adf07f86","timestamp":"2026-09-05T04:10:59.229Z"}
